  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "Regular -ir verbs in Spanish share the same present tense endings as -er verbs, with one important difference: in the first-person plural (nosotros/nosotras) form the theme vowel changes to -i-, giving the ending -imos. For example, the verb vivir (to live) is conjugated as vivo, vives, vive, vivimos, viven. All first-person singular forms end in -o regardless of the theme vowel. The person–number endings (-s, -mos, -n) are the same as those for -ar and -er verbs."
    }
